==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|líða|lang=non}}, from {{proto|Germanic|līþanan|lang=is}}. The senses “suffer, tolerate” may be borrowed from {{etyl|gml|is}}, but derive from the same root in any case.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈliːða/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|iːða|lang=is}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|leið|liðu|liðið}}

# {{context|transitive|governs the dative|of time}} to [[pass]], to [[go by]]{{jump|is|pass|d}}
#: ''Ætluðum við ekki að hittast í vikunni sem '''leið'''?''
#:: Weren't we going to meet '''last''' week?
#: ''Tíminn '''líður'''.''
#:: Time '''goes by'''.
#: ''Þegar '''leið''' á daginn heyrðu þeir í drauginum sem bjó í fjallinu.''
#:: They heard the ghost in the mountain as the day grew old.
# {{context|intransitive}} to [[float]], to [[glide]]{{jump|is|glide|s}}
# {{context|impersonal|intransitive|lang=is}} describing a specific [[feeling]]; to [[feel]] {{jump|is|feel|s}}
#: ''Hvernig '''líður''' þér? - ''Mér '''líður''' ekki vel.''
#:: How are you '''feeling'''? - I don't '''feel''' good.
#: ''Mér '''líður''' vel.''
#:: I '''feel''' good.
#: ''Okkur '''líður''' illa.''
#:: We '''feel''' bad.''
# {{context|ambitransitive|governs the dative}} to [[progress]]{{jump|is|progress|s}}
#: ''Hvernig '''líður''' náminu?''
#:: How are your '''studies''' progressing?
# {{context|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[suffer]]{{jump|is|suffer|s}}
#: ''Þú munt '''líða''' fyrir það sem vinir þínir gerðu.''
#:: You shall '''suffer''' for what your friends did.
# {{context|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[endure]], to [[tolerate]]{{jump|is|tolerate|s}}
#: ''Ég '''líð''' ekki svona vitleysu!''
#:: I do not '''tolerate''' this kind of nonsense!

